+6. **Reduce the Trigger** (when the symptom is gated by input or configuration)
+
+   **WHEN the bug appears with one input/config/environment and not another** --
+   "works here, breaks there," toggles with a flag/plugin/trusted-mode, fires on
+   one input but not a similar one.
+
+   See `reducing-the-trigger.md` in this directory for the complete technique. It is
+   the *subtractive* peer to root-cause-tracing: instead of tracing a bad value
+   backward, shrink the failing case (bisect the environment, then delta-minimize
+   the input) until one-bit difference between ON and OFF names the cause. Needs no
+   understanding of the mechanism.
+
+   **Quick version:**
+   - A config/input that reliably toggles the symptom is EVIDENCE -- chase it.
+   - Get a reliable ON and OFF, then bisect the difference.
+   - Build the repro empty-up (minimal known-good + add until it breaks), NOT
+     cloned-down (full failing env - subtract), or you may never observe OFF.
 
