 **But:** 95% of "no root cause" cases are incomplete investigation.
 
+**Before you accept "environmental," make the tool say WHY.** "Fails
+environmentally, ignore" earns no more trust than any other unexplained signal.
+Get the exact error code / decline reason / exit status out of the failing tool,
+then bisect the trigger (see `reducing-the-trigger.md`). "Environmental" failures
+routinely turn out to have a concrete, fixable cause once the tool is made to
+explain itself.
+
 ## Supporting Techniques
 
 These techniques are part of systematic debugging and available in this directory:
 
 - **`root-cause-tracing.md`** - Trace bugs backward through call stack to find original trigger
+- **`reducing-the-trigger.md`** - Subtractive peer to tracing: when the symptom is gated by input/config, bisect and delta-minimize until a one-bit difference names the cause
 - **`defense-in-depth.md`** - Add validation at multiple layers after finding root cause
 - **`condition-based-waiting.md`** - Replace arbitrary timeouts with condition polling
 
